  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What moves",
      "items": [
        "Outputs (face, gaze, colour, say, torch, vibrate) go from the setup page through /api/act onto the contract's own ROS topics, so the test runs the same chain a robot program would.",
        "Senses go the other way: WebSocket frame → protocol.parse → ROS publisher, and a copy into seen for the setup page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "/api/state and /api/act answer loopback only; /ws and /report refuse a foreign Origin (wsserver.py 234–243).",
        "A phone over plain http says secure: false in hello; the setup page then shows camera, motion, compass and battery as blocked, not failed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Wi-Fi over HTTPS",
      "items": [
        "./start.sh --make-cert makes this PC's certificate authority once and the bridge's certificate for its addresses (renewed when the address changes). Only cert.pem, key.pem and ca.crt are mounted; ca.key stays in certs/.",
        "The bridge offers the authority at GET /ca.crt; the setup page's Wi-Fi tab has its QR code and the install steps. With a certificate the bridge speaks https only, over USB too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading this",
      "items": [
        "The phone check (check.html) is optional; its report comes back by POST /report and is kept (the last 10).",
        "Paths cite commit 6b29b5a; the repository is local only (not pushed)."
      ]
    }
  ]
